%description:

Tcp.keepAliveInterval:other -- an unanswered probe is followed by the next one 2 s later.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the time between two keepalive probes (Linux tcp_keepalive_intvl)".

The classes: linux (75 s, the default, the value of Linux tcp_keepalive_intvl) and other
(another value). The code: TcpAlgorithmBase::processKeepAliveTimer() schedules the next probe
the value after a probe. This test separates "other" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, with keepalive and an idle time of 1 s (preconditions); host1 sends 10000 bytes at 0.2 s and then nothing; host2 sends nothing. A keepalive probe is a
segment without data with SEG.SEQ = SND.UNA - 1. The tap drops
each segment of host2 after the data, so no probe gets an answer. Observation: level 1, the
second probe comes 2 s after the first, and not before.

%# parameter: Tcp.keepAliveInterval
%# class: other
%# value: 2s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.keepAliveInterval
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpKeepAliveIntervalOther")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 10000")
             .describe("the ACK of all data of host1: the idle time starts")
             .within(1.0))
        .meanwhile(tap("tap").from("host2").drop()
                       .describe("each segment of host2 after the data: the probes get no answer"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 10000 && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the first keepalive probe")
             .within(1.1))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 10000 && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("an early second keepalive probe")
              .within(1.9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 10000 && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("second keepalive probe")
             .within(0.2));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpKeepAliveIntervalOther compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveInterval = 2s    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveIdleTime = 1s
sim-time-limit = 5s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpKeepAliveIntervalOther: PASS
